From f678b5819df86daac00719e6b10aac8ef1a08eb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <19559105+ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x86: guarded-loop LEA hoist, direct 3-operand RORX
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Loop-instruction-quality delta on top of the FP-call-staging work that is
already on main (#586). Three changes, one new CI gate, plus the review
follow-up hardening:

1. Loop-invariant LEA hoisting for guard/fall-through-entry loops
   (local_patterns.rs): hoist_loop_invariant_gpr_load previously required a
   jmp-entry preheader and skipped guarded loops entirely. A guarded loop
   (cmp; jcc exit; .p2align; header:) now admits PURE-LEA candidates only:
   a LEA touches no memory and writes no flags, so it is safe to execute on
   the zero-iteration path. Placement is inserted directly after the last
   control-flow boundary above the header's directive run, keeping the
   alignment directives adjacent to the header label. loop_entry_is_unique
   gains a fallthrough_ok mode (zero jump edges is the unique entry).
   One candidate per loop per pass; after insertion i/len are re-adjusted
   and a classified LineInfo is spliced so infos.len() == store.len().

2. LineStore::insert_line (peephole_common.rs): the structural insertion
   primitive backing (1) — lands the text in the replacements arena as a
   REPLACED-style entry; O(len) splice, no original-buffer surgery.

3. Direct 3-operand RORX (emit.rs): constant rotates at width 32/64 with
   BMI2 now read a provably-fresh register home in place — RORX is
   non-destructive, so the staged movq into the destination is deleted
   from the hot path (`rorxl $k, %r14d, %ebp` instead of movq + rorxl).
   sha256's sigma loops staged a movq before every rorxl (~3 dead moves
   per round, ~192 per transform). Falls back to the staged form when the
   home is clobbered/absent; RotateLeft maps to width-amount; the sext32
   normalization for signed 32-bit results is preserved.

Review follow-up (the first push of this PR, 9eefe9e, double-applied two
hunks whose content had already landed on main via #586 — the six
fp_liveness unit tests and the simplify float sub-neg fold — producing
E0428 duplicate definitions and red Clippy/Test jobs):

- Both files are restored to their 156c4eb (post-#586) state; per-hunk
  duplicate-content probes confirm every test fn and the fold block now
  exist exactly once. The true delta of this PR is the 6 files above.

- The fall-through placement boundary set is narrowed to CondJmp | Label:
  an unconditional-jmp boundary cuts the fall-through, and the zero-entry
  requirement already proves such a loop unreachable — an insertion there
  would be dead code dressed up as a hoist. (Fail-closed narrowing; the
  K-table guarded shape is a CondJmp boundary and is unaffected.)

- Seven unit pins for the fall-through insertion mechanics in
  loop_hoist_tests, previously covered only by the shell gate: the golden
  placement (guard < LEA < .p2align < header, alignment adjacency), the
  Label-boundary placement, the zero-trip LOAD refusal, the
  unconditional-jmp boundary refusal (discriminating — it fails on the
  pre-narrowing tree, negative-verified), the base/index LEA refusal,
  the second-entry refusal, and Rule 5 through the insert path.

tests/regression/check_lea_hoist_rorx.sh (new, executable) gates both
instruction-quality contracts and is wired into .github/workflows/ci.yml
and scripts/ci_local.sh next to the existing call-arg-staging gate.

Verification (full local battery on this tree): cargo test --profile
fastbuild --all-targets --locked 3129/0 (7 new pins included); clippy
--all-targets --profile fastbuild --locked -D warnings clean; cargo fmt
clean; regression corpus 768 passed / 3 known-environmental i686 multilib
link failures (the oracle gcc cannot link ELF32 locally) / 22 skip;
benchmark output oracle 204/204; differential correctness 57/57;
lea-hoist/rorx gate 7/7; call-arg-staging 5/5; vector-copy-elim 46/46;
vectorize ISA gate, peephole phi-hoist, cross-PR red-team (4 configs x 2
batteries), const-array, range-fold, replay-gap, loop-memset, bool-pair
x2, kernel-tool-identity, loop-alignment and CI-gate-parity all PASS.

